A||||3||My7Fieros||WOW! What happened?!!||||10||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||11-12-2000||02:14 PM||||Well I went out to get in my Formula last night and WHAMMO! Flat tire! S%@T! Oh well, I filled it up and decided it was time to put new ones on (all the tires were dry rotted "maypops"...may pop at any time).<BR>WOW! This may sound dumb, but I swear that car is 10 times easier to drive now! Its really hard to explain. Its the only 88 Ive got and Ive always heard people talking about how much better they drive and handle (dont start the "lotus" thing please!), but I always thought that it drove like a truck compared to my 86's and 87's. The tires that were on it were old and dryrotted, half inflated constantly, and basically crappy.<BR>What a diff! Can tires alone make that much difference? BTW, they're Bridgestone Pontenzas 205's all the way around (they didnt have 215s). <p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 11-12-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Black88GT||11-12-2000||03:13 PM||||Same thing happened with me.  The previous owner was too cheap to get decent tires, at the same time.  There were like 4 different brands with 4 different tread depths, not to mention the wrong size for the front.  Got new BFG Comp. T/A's and handling was like night and day.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||11-12-2000||05:44 PM||||Yep, tires can make a huge difference in handling. I've done the same thing with past project cars too and was amazed how much better they ride with new high-quality rubber.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/batkid3.gif">   <B>BATBOY</B><BR>1985 SE auto with 350 Chevy V8 (Batmobile),<BR>suspension mods, lowered, GA brakes, etc...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero5||11-12-2000||07:29 PM||||My 87 crab walked alot until I changed to better tires. Huge difference.||||reg||1
